"fontSize":"18px"},"children":"AI in China"}],["$","$L2",null,{"href":"/blog/","style":{"color":"#a3a3a3","textDecoration":"none","fontSize":"14px"},"children":"Blog"}]]}]}],["$","article",null,{"style":{"maxWidth":"800px","margin":"0 auto","padding":"48px 24px"},"children":[["$","header",null,{"style":{"marginBottom":"48px"},"children":[["$","div",null,{"style":{"display":"flex","gap":"12px","marginBottom":"24px","flexWrap":"wrap"},"children":[["$","span",null,{"style":{"backgroundColor":"#1a1a1a","padding":"6px 12px","borderRadius":"6px","fontSize":"12px","fontWeight":"600","color":"#22d3ee","textTransform":"uppercase","letterSpacing":"0.05em"},"children":"AI"}],["$","span",null,{"style":{"backgroundColor":"#1a1a1a","padding":"6px 12px","borderRadius":"6px","fontSize":"12px","color":"#737373"},"children":"16 min read"}]]}],["$","h1",null,{"style":{"fontSize":"36px","fontWeight":"700","lineHeight":"1.2","margin":"0 0 24px","color":"#f5f5f5"},"children":"GLM-5.1: The 754B-Parameter Open-Source MoE That Beat GPT-5.4 on Real-World Coding — and Trained Without NVIDIA"}],["$","div",null,{"style":{"display":"flex","alignItems":"center","gap":"16px","color":"#737373","fontSize":"14px"},"children":[["$","span",null,{"children":"June 13, 2026"}],["$","span",null,{"children":"·"}],["$","span",null,{"children":"AI in China"}]]}]]}],["$","img",null,{"src":"https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1633356122544-f134324a6cee?w=1200","alt":"GLM-5.1: The 754B-Parameter Open-Source MoE That Beat GPT-5.4 on Real-World Coding — and Trained Without NVIDIA","style":{"width":"100%","height":"auto","borderRadius":"12px","marginBottom":"48px"}}],["$","div",null,{"children":[["$","p","0",{"style":{"fontSize":"16px","lineHeight":"1.8","margin":"16px 0","color":"#e5e5e5"},"children":[["$","span","0",{"children":"heroImage: \"https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1485827404703-89b55fcc595e?w=1200\""}]]}],["$","p","5",{"style":{"fontSize":"16px","lineHeight":"1.8","margin":"16px 0","color":"#e5e5e5"},"children":[["$","span","0",{"children":"On April 7, 2026, a Chinese AI research lab quietly uploaded a set of model weights to Hugging Face. There was no splashy livestream. No Sam Altman tweet thread. No carefully choreographed product demo. Just a repository named `zai-org/GLM-5` and a one-line release note: \"GLM-5.1 is now available under the MIT License.\""}]]}],["$","p","7",{"style":{"fontSize":"16px","lineHeight":"1.8","margin":"16px 0","color":"#e5e5e5"},"children":[["$","span","0",{"children":"Within 72 hours, the global developer community realized something extraordinary had happened. GLM-5.1 — a 754-billion-parameter Mixture-of-Experts model built by Z.ai, the research arm of Zhipu AI — had achieved a score of "}],["$","strong","1",{"style":{"color":"#f5f5f5","fontWeight":"700"},"children":"58.4 on SWE-Bench Pro"}],["$","span","2",{"children":", the industry's most rigorous benchmark for real-world software engineering. That score placed it ahead of GPT-5.4 (57.7), Claude Opus 4.6 (57.3), and Gemini 3.1 Pro (54.2). For the first time in the history of frontier AI, an open-source model had surpassed every closed-source competitor on a benchmark that tests actual code repair in real open-source repositories."}]]}],["$","p","9",{"style":{"fontSize":"16px","lineHeight":"1.8","margin":"16px 0","color":"#e5e5e5"},"children":[["$","span","0",{"children":"The conventional wisdom in Silicon Valley holds that open-source AI leadership belongs to Western institutions — Meta's Llama family, Google's Gemma, Mistral's European engineering. The corollary assumption is that Chinese AI labs, cut off from the most advanced NVIDIA chips by US export restrictions, cannot compete at the frontier of model capability. GLM-5.1 shatters both assumptions simultaneously. Not only did it top the global leaderboard, but it was trained entirely on "}],["$","strong","1",{"style":{"color":"#f5f5f5","fontWeight":"700"},"children":"Huawei Ascend 910B chips"}],["$","span","2",{"children":" using the MindSpore framework — with zero NVIDIA hardware involvement."}]]}],["$","p","11",{"style":{"fontSize":"16px","lineHeight":"1.8","margin":"16px 0","color":"#e5e5e5"},"children":[["$","span","0",{"children":"This is not merely a technical achievement. It is a structural signal that the geography of open-source AI leadership is being redrawn in real time."}]]}],["$","h2","13",{"style":{"fontSize":"28px","fontWeight":"600","margin":"40px 0 20px","color":"#f5f5f5"},"children":[["$","span","0",{"children":"The Benchmark That Matters: Why SWE-Bench Pro Is Different"}]]}],["$","p","15",{"style":{"fontSize":"16px","lineHeight":"1.8","margin":"16px 0","color":"#e5e5e5"},"children":[["$","span","0",{"children":"Most AI benchmarks test what models know. SWE-Bench Pro tests what models can actually do. Developed by researchers at Princeton and OpenAI, the benchmark presents models with real bug reports from GitHub repositories and asks them to write patches that fix the issue. The model must read the codebase, understand the problem, write code, and verify that the fix works. It is not a multiple-choice test. It is a practical engineering exam."}]]}],["$","p","17",{"style":{"fontSize":"16px","lineHeight":"1.8","margin":"16px 0","color":"#e5e5e5"},"children":[["$","span","0",{"children":"Before GLM-5.1, the top of the SWE-Bench Pro leaderboard was dominated by closed-source models with multimillion-dollar training budgets and exclusive access to the latest NVIDIA clusters. GPT-5.4 held the crown at 57.7. Claude Opus 4.6 followed at 57.3. The best open-source model, Kimi K2.6 from Moonshot AI, had reached 58.4 — but Kimi K2.6 was released two weeks later, on April 20, creating a brief period where GLM-5.1 stood alone at the top."}]]}],["$","p","19",{"style":{"fontSize":"16px","lineHeight":"1.8","margin":"16px 0","color":"#e5e5e5"},"children":[["$","span","0",{"children":"What makes GLM-5.1's achievement particularly striking is the architecture. While GPT-5.4 and Claude Opus 4.6 are dense models trained on proprietary infrastructure with effectively unlimited budgets, GLM-5.1 is a Mixture-of-Experts design with only 40 billion active parameters per token. The full 754 billion parameters are never activated simultaneously. This sparse architecture keeps inference costs manageable while delivering frontier capability — a efficiency advantage that closed-source competitors cannot easily replicate."}]]}],["$","h2","21",{"style":{"fontSize":"28px","fontWeight":"600","margin":"40px 0 20px","color":"#f5f5f5"},"children":[["$","span","0",{"children":"GLM-5.1: Technical Architecture and Capabilities"}]]}],["$","p","23",{"style":{"fontSize":"16px","lineHeight":"1.8","margin":"16px 0","color":"#e5e5e5"},"children":[["$","span","0",{"children":"To understand why GLM-5.1 represents a qualitative leap, it is necessary to examine the specifications in detail. The model is not merely a scaled-up version of its predecessor. It introduces several architectural innovations that specifically target the gap between open-source and closed-source performance on agentic tasks."}]]}],["$","div","35",{"style":{"overflowX":"auto","margin":"24px 0"},"children":["$","table",null,{"style":{"width":"100%","borderCollapse":"collapse","fontSize":"14px"},"children":[["$","thead",null,{"children":["$","tr",null,{"children":[["$","th","0",{"style":{"borderBottom":"2px solid #22d3ee","padding":"12px 16px","textAlign":"left","fontWeight":"600","color":"#22d3ee"},"children":[["$","span","0",{"children":"Specification"}]]}],["$","th","1",{"style":{"borderBottom":"2px solid #22d3ee","padding":"12px 16px","textAlign":"left","fontWeight":"600","color":"#22d3ee"},"children":[["$","span","0",{"children":"GLM-5.1"}]]}],["$","th","2",{"style":{"borderBottom":"2px solid #22d3ee","padding":"12px 16px","textAlign":"left","fontWeight":"600","color":"#22d3ee"},"children":[["$","span","0",{"children":"GPT-5.4"}]]}],["$","th","3",{"style":{"borderBottom":"2px solid #22d3ee","padding":"12px 16px","textAlign":"left","fontWeight":"600","color":"#22d3ee"},"children":[["$","span","0",{"children":"Claude Opus 4.6"}]]}],["$","th","4",{"style":{"borderBottom":"2px solid #22d3ee","padding":"12px 16px","textAlign":"left","fontWeight":"600","color":"#22d3ee"},"children":[["$","span","0",{"children":"Kimi K2.6"}]]}]]}]}],["$","tbody",null,{"children":[["$","tr","0",{"children":[["$","td","0",{"style":{"borderBottom":"1px solid #1a1a1a","padding":"12px 16px","color":"#e5e5e5"},"children":[["$","strong","0",{"style":{"color":"#f5f5f5","fontWeight":"700"},"children":"Total Parameters"}]]}],["$","td","1",{"style":{"borderBottom":"1px solid #1a1a1a","padding":"12px 16px","color":"#e5e5e5"},"children":[["$","span","0",{"children":"754B (MoE)"}]]}],["$","td","2",{"style":{"borderBottom":"1px solid #1a1a1a","padding":"12px 16px","color":"#e5e5e5"},"children":[["$","span","0",{"children":"~1.8T (dense)"}]]}],["$","td","3",{"style":{"borderBottom":"1px solid #1a1a1a","padding":"12px 16px","color":"#e5e5e5"},"children":[["$","span","0",{"children":"~1.5T (dense)"}]]}],["$","td","4",{"style":{"borderBottom":"1px solid #1a1a1a","padding":"12px 16px","color":"#e5e5e5"},"children":[["$","span","0",{"children":"1T (MoE)"}]]}]]}],["$","tr","1",{"children":[["$","td","0",{"style":{"borderBottom":"1px solid #1a1a1a","padding":"12px 16px","color":"#e5e5e5"},"children":[["$","strong","0",{"style":{"color":"#f5f5f5","fontWeight":"700"},"children":"Active Parameters per Token"}]]}],["$","td","1",{"style":{"borderBottom":"1px solid #1a1a1a","padding":"12px 16px","color":"#e5e5e5"},"children":[["$","span","0",{"children":"~40B"}]]}],["$","td","2",{"style":{"borderBottom":"1px solid #1a1a1a","padding":"12px 16px","color":"#e5e5e5"},"children":[["$","span","0",{"children":"~1.8T"}]]}],["$","td","3",{"style":{"borderBottom":"1px solid #1a1a1a","padding":"12px 16px","color":"#e5e5e5"},"children":[["$","span","0",{"children":"~1.5T"}]]}],["$","td","4",{"style":{"borderBottom":"1px solid #1a1a1a","padding":"12px 16px","color":"#e5e5e5"},"children":[["$","span","0",{"children":"~32B"}]]}]]}],["$","tr","2",{"children":[["$","td","0",{"style":{"borderBottom":"1px solid #1a1a1a","padding":"12px 16px","color":"#e5e5e5"},"children":[["$","strong","0",{"style":{"color":"#f5f5f5","fontWeight":"700"},"children":"Context Window"}]]}],["$","td","1",{"style":{"borderBottom":"1px solid #1a1a1a","padding":"12px 16px","color":"#e5e5e5"},"children":[["$","span","0",{"children":"200,000 tokens"}]]}],["$","td","2",{"style":{"borderBottom":"1px solid #1a1a1a","padding":"12px 16px","color":"#e5e5e5"},"children":[["$","span","0",{"children":"256,000 tokens"}]]}],["$","td","3",{"style":{"borderBottom":"1px solid #1a1a1a","padding":"12px 16px","color":"#e5e5e5"},"children":[["$","span","0",{"children":"200,000 tokens"}]]}],["$","td","4",{"style":{"borderBottom":"1px solid #1a1a1a","padding":"12px 16px","color":"#e5e5e5"},"children":[["$","span","0",{"children":"256,000 tokens"}]]}]]}],["$","tr","3",{"children":[["$","td","0",{"style":{"borderBottom":"1px solid #1a1a1a","padding":"12px 16px","color":"#e5e5e5"},"children":[["$","strong","0",{"style":{"color":"#f5f5f5","fontWeight":"700"},"children":"Max Output Length"}]]}],["$","td","1",{"style":{"borderBottom":"1px solid #1a1a1a","padding":"12px 16px","color":"#e5e5e5"},"children":[["$","span","0",{"children":"128,000 tokens"}]]}],["$","td","2",{"style":{"borderBottom":"1px solid #1a1a1a","padding":"12px 16px","color":"#e5e5e5"},"children":[["$","span","0",{"children":"128,000 tokens"}]]}],["$","td","3",{"style":{"borderBottom":"1px solid #1a1a1a","padding":"12px 16px","color":"#e5e5e5"},"children":[["$","span","0",{"children":"128,000 tokens"}]]}],["$","td","4",{"style":{"borderBottom":"1px solid #1a1a1a","padding":"12px 16px","color":"#e5e5e5"},"children":[["$","span","0",{"children":"128,000 tokens"}]]}]]}],["$","tr","4",{"children":[["$","td","0",{"style":{"borderBottom":"1px solid #1a1a1a","padding":"12px 16px","color":"#e5e5e5"},"children":[["$","strong","0",{"style":{"color":"#f5f5f5","fontWeight":"700"},"children":"SWE-Bench Pro"}]]}],["$","td","1",{"style":{"borderBottom":"1px solid #1a1a1a","padding":"12px 16px","color":"#e5e5e5"},"children":[["$","span","0",{"children":"58.4%"}]]}],["$","td","2",{"style":{"borderBottom":"1px solid #1a1a1a","padding":"12px 16px","color":"#e5e5e5"},"children":[["$","span","0",{"children":"57.7%"}]]}],["$","td","3",{"style":{"borderBottom":"1px solid #1a1a1a","padding":"12px 16px","color":"#e5e5e5"},"children":[["$","span","0",{"children":"57.3%"}]]}],["$","td","4",{"style":{"borderBottom":"1px solid #1a1a1a","padding":"12px 16px","color":"#e5e5e5"},"children":[["$","span","0",{"children":"58.4%"}]]}]]}],["$","tr","5",{"children":[["$","td","0",{"style":{"borderBottom":"1px solid #1a1a1a","padding":"12px 16px","color":"#e5e5e5"},"children":[["$","strong","0",{"style":{"color":"#f5f5f5","fontWeight":"700"},"children":"Training Data"}]]}],["$","td","1",{"style":{"borderBottom":"1px solid #1a1a1a","padding":"12px 16px","color":"#e5e5e5"},"children":[["$","span","0",{"children":"28.5T tokens"}]]}],["$","td","2",{"style":{"borderBottom":"1px solid #1a1a1a","padding":"12px 16px","color":"#e5e5e5"},"children":[["$","span","0",{"children":"Undisclosed"}]]}],["$","td","3",{"style":{"borderBottom":"1px solid #1a1a1a","padding":"12px 16px","color":"#e5e5e5"},"children":[["$","span","0",{"children":"Undisclosed"}]]}],["$","td","4",{"style":{"borderBottom":"1px solid #1a1a1a","padding":"12px 16px","color":"#e5e5e5"},"children":[["$","span","0",{"children":"Undisclosed"}]]}]]}],["$","tr","6",{"children":[["$","td","0",{"style":{"borderBottom":"1px solid #1a1a1a","padding":"12px 16px","color":"#e5e5e5"},"children":[["$","strong","0",{"style":{"color":"#f5f5f5","fontWeight":"700"},"children":"License"}]]}],["$","td","1",{"style":{"borderBottom":"1px solid #1a1a1a","padding":"12px 16px","color":"#e5e5e5"},"children":[["$","span","0",{"children":"MIT"}]]}],["$","td","2",{"style":{"borderBottom":"1px solid #1a1a1a","padding":"12px 16px","color":"#e5e5e5"},"children":[["$","span","0",{"children":"Proprietary"}]]}],["$","td","3",{"style":{"borderBottom":"1px solid #1a1a1a","padding":"12px 16px","color":"#e5e5e5"},"children":[["$","span","0",{"children":"Proprietary"}]]}],["$","td","4",{"style":{"borderBottom":"1px solid #1a1a1a","padding":"12px 16px","color":"#e5e5e5"},"children":[["$","span","0",{"children":"Open-weight"}]]}]]}],["$","tr","7",{"children":[["$","td","0",{"style":{"borderBottom":"1px solid #1a1a1a","padding":"12px 16px","color":"#e5e5e5"},"children":[["$","strong","0",{"style":{"color":"#f5f5f5","fontWeight":"700"},"children":"Training Hardware"}]]}],["$","td","1",{"style":{"borderBottom":"1px solid #1a1a1a","padding":"12px 16px","color":"#e5e5e5"},"children":[["$","span","0",{"children":"Huawei Ascend 910B"}]]}],["$","td","2",{"style":{"borderBottom":"1px solid #1a1a1a","padding":"12px 16px","color":"#e5e5e5"},"children":[["$","span","0",{"children":"NVIDIA H100/H200"}]]}],["$","td","3",{"style":{"borderBottom":"1px solid #1a1a1a","padding":"12px 16px","color":"#e5e5e5"},"children":[["$","span","0",{"children":"NVIDIA H100"}]]}],["$","td","4",{"style":{"borderBottom":"1px solid #1a1a1a","padding":"12px 16px","color":"#e5e5e5"},"children":[["$","span","0",{"children":"NVIDIA H100"}]]}]]}]]}]]}]}],["$","p","36",{"style":{"fontSize":"16px","lineHeight":"1.8","margin":"16px 0","color":"#e5e5e5"},"children":[["$","span","0",{"children":"*Data compiled from Z.ai technical documentation, OpenAI specifications, Anthropic release notes, and Moonshot AI reports (April-June 2026)*"}]]}],["$","p","38",{"style":{"fontSize":"16px","lineHeight":"1.8","margin":"16px 0","color":"#e5e5e5"},"children":[["$","span","0",{"children":"The most significant specification is not a single number but a combination: 754 billion parameters with only 40 billion active per token, a 200,000-token context window, and an MIT license. This combination means that GLM-5.1 can be deployed by any organization, modified for any use case, and run at inference costs that are a fraction of what dense models of equivalent capability would require."}]]}],["$","h3","40",{"style":{"fontSize":"22px","fontWeight":"600","margin":"32px 0 16px","color":"#f5f5f5"},"children":[["$","span","0",{"children":"The 8-Hour Autonomy Breakthrough"}]]}],["$","p","42",{"style":{"fontSize":"16px","lineHeight":"1.8","margin":"16px 0","color":"#e5e5e5"},"children":[["$","span","0",{"children":"Beyond benchmark scores, GLM-5.1 introduces a capability that fundamentally changes how developers can use AI models: sustained autonomous execution. In demonstrations, the model has been shown to work on a single coding task for up to "}],["$","strong","1",{"style":{"color":"#f5f5f5","fontWeight":"700"},"children":"eight hours"}],["$","span","2",{"children":" without human intervention — planning, executing, testing, debugging, and iterating across hundreds of tool calls. In one documented session, GLM-5.1 made over 6,000 tool calls to build a vector database from scratch, achieving 21,500 queries per second."}]]}],["$","p","44",{"style":{"fontSize":"16px","lineHeight":"1.8","margin":"16px 0","color":"#e5e5e5"},"children":[["$","span","0",{"children":"This \"marathon runner\" architecture contrasts sharply with the \"sprinter\" models that dominate consumer AI interfaces. Most chat models are optimized for short, single-turn interactions. They excel at answering questions but struggle with tasks that require sustained reasoning over hours. GLM-5.1 was explicitly designed for the latter: long-horizon agentic workflows where the model must maintain context, adapt its strategy, and recover from errors over extended time periods."}]]}],["$","div","53",{"style":{"overflowX":"auto","margin":"24px 0"},"children":["$","table",null,{"style":{"width":"100%","borderCollapse":"collapse","fontSize":"14px"},"children":[["$","thead",null,{"children":["$","tr",null,{"children":[["$","th","0",{"style":{"borderBottom":"2px solid #22d3ee","padding":"12px 16px","textAlign":"left","fontWeight":"600","color":"#22d3ee"},"children":[["$","span","0",{"children":"Capability"}]]}],["$","th","1",{"style":{"borderBottom":"2px solid #22d3ee","padding":"12px 16px","textAlign":"left","fontWeight":"600","color":"#22d3ee"},"children":[["$","span","0",{"children":"GLM-5.1"}]]}],["$","th","2",{"style":{"borderBottom":"2px solid #22d3ee","padding":"12px 16px","textAlign":"left","fontWeight":"600","color":"#22d3ee"},"children":[["$","span","0",{"children":"Industry Standard"}]]}],["$","th","3",{"style":{"borderBottom":"2px solid #22d3ee","padding":"12px 16px","textAlign":"left","fontWeight":"600","color":"#22d3ee"},"children":[["$","span","0",{"children":"Significance"}]]}]]}]}],["$","tbody",null,{"children":[["$","tr","0",{"children":[["$","td","0",{"style":{"borderBottom":"1px solid #1a1a1a","padding":"12px 16px","color":"#e5e5e5"},"children":[["$","strong","0",{"style":{"color":"#f5f5f5","fontWeight":"700"},"children":"Autonomous Work Duration"}]]}],["$","td","1",{"style":{"borderBottom":"1px solid #1a1a1a","padding":"12px 16px","color":"#e5e5e5"},"children":[["$","span","0",{"children":"Up to 8 hours"}]]}],["$","td","2",{"style":{"borderBottom":"1px solid #1a1a1a","padding":"12px 16px","color":"#e5e5e5"},"children":[["$","span","0",{"children":"5-30 minutes"}]]}],["$","td","3",{"style":{"borderBottom":"1px solid #1a1a1a","padding":"12px 16px","color":"#e5e5e5"},"children":[["$","span","0",{"children":"First open model with sustained agentic capability"}]]}]]}],["$","tr","1",{"children":[["$","td","0",{"style":{"borderBottom":"1px solid #1a1a1a","padding":"12px 16px","color":"#e5e5e5"},"children":[["$","strong","0",{"style":{"color":"#f5f5f5","fontWeight":"700"},"children":"Tool Calls per Session"}]]}],["$","td","1",{"style":{"borderBottom":"1px solid #1a1a1a","padding":"12px 16px","color":"#e5e5e5"},"children":[["$","span","0",{"children"